  "theory": {
"intro": "Ten per cent is one tenth, so finding $10\\%$ of an amount means dividing it by $10$.",
"facts": [
      "$10\\% = \\dfrac{10}{100} = \\dfrac{1}{10}$.",
      "$10\\%$ of an amount $=$ amount $\\div 10$.",
      "Once you have $10\\%$, you can double it for $20\\%$ or halve it for $5\\%$."
    ],
"steps": [
"Find $10\\%$ by dividing the whole amount by $10$: one tenth of the whole.",
"For $20\\%$, double the $10\\%$ amount. For $5\\%$, halve it.",
"For $15\\%$, add the $10\\%$ amount and the $5\\%$ amount.",
"Keep the units and check that each share makes sense compared with its whole."
],
